IMPORT prelude

-- Building Act 2011 (Western Australia) -- the home owner building a house: do I need a building permit, who applies and
-- signs, where the certificate of design compliance comes from, must the permit be granted, what happens if I build without
-- one, what I must do at completion, and whether the new house must have an occupancy permit before we move in.
--
-- SEAT: the home owner building a house -- an "owner" of the land (s 5(1): "a person whose name is registered as a
-- proprietor of the land ... a person who holds a prescribed interest in the land"). Every exported question is phrased as
-- that owner would ask it. Where the Act addresses only the permit authority (ss 17, 20, 23, 24, 58), the building surveyor
-- (ss 4, 19) or the builder (ss 29, 33, 34, 37(1)), what is encoded is what the owner must be given, what may be done to the
-- owner, and what the owner may do about it. An owner who is also the person named as the builder on the permit (an
-- owner-builder) carries the builder's duties too.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 3 ("building work", "incidental structure", "building permit", "occupancy permit"); s 4
-- (independent building surveyor); s 5 (owner); s 9 (no building work without a building permit) and its penalty; ss 11,
-- 12 (defences, as inputs); s 14 (certified and uncertified applications); s 16(b), (c), (e), (h), (j), (k) (who signs, what
-- accompanies); s 17 (uncertified application referred to a building surveyor); s 19(3) (what the certificate of design
-- compliance states); s 20 (grant of building permit); s 23 (time to decide, deemed refusal, refund); s 24 (notice of
-- refusal within 5 days); s 28(1)(b), (2A) (permit given to each owner); s 32(2) (2-year duration); s 33 (notice of
-- completion within 7 days); s 34(3) (owner's copy of a notice of cessation); s 37 (building standards at completion,
-- including the owner's duty where there was no permit); s 40 (occupier); s 41 (occupancy permit before occupation) and its
-- penalty; ss 46, 47, 51, 54 (occupancy permit applications and the certificate that accompanies them); s 63 (permit given
-- to each owner); s 69 (temporary buildings); s 119 (review by the State Administrative Tribunal); s 133(3), (4)
-- (prosecution time limits).
--
-- Edition: compilation of the Building Act 2011 (Act No. 24 of 2011) as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49441.txt (legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc 49441, retrieved 2026-09-07). The latest
-- amendment noted in the text read is No. 14 of 2025 (s 19). Regulations: the Building Regulations 2012 are NOT deposited.
-- Every number or class they set is an input: which classifications may use an uncertified application (s 14(2)), the
-- period to decide an application (s 23), the buildings that need no building permit or no occupancy permit (s 66(1),
-- (5)), and the "prescribed interest" that makes a person an owner (s 5).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: demolition permits (ss 10, 15, 21, 38) except that demolition is not building work; staged permits (s 26);
-- the builder's display duty (s 30); suspension (s 35) beyond the s 11 defence; inspections (s 36); the Building
-- Commissioner's declarations (s 39); the owner's duties under an occupancy permit already in effect (ss 42-44) and
-- building safety regulations (s 45); modification, replacement and extension of occupancy permits (ss 48, 49, 52, 64, 65);
-- the infrastructure, shipping, mining, petroleum and plant exemptions (ss 70-74); work affecting other land (Part 6);
-- existing buildings (Part 7); authorised persons, entry and building orders (Part 8) except that work under a building
-- order needs no permit; permit authorities, records and evidence (Parts 10-13); transitional provisions (Part 16).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the home owner building a house, with the
-- design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Building Act 2011 -- the home owner building a house`

§§ `the work, the owner, the surveyor`

-- s 3: "building work means -- (a) the construction, erection, assembly or placement of a building or an incidental
-- structure; or (b) the renovation, alteration, extension, improvement or repair of a building or an incidental structure;
-- or (c) the assembly, reassembly or securing of a relocated building ...; or (d) the changing of ground levels ... ; or
-- (e) site work on any land for the purposes of ... work of a kind mentioned in (a), (b), (c) or (d) ...; or (f) other
-- prescribed work, but does not include work of a kind prescribed ... as not being building work". "incidental structure"
-- includes "a chimney, mast, swimming pool, fence, freestanding wall, retaining wall". Demolition is "demolition work",
-- a separate definition. Which the work is, is a FACT the owner states.
DECLARE `Kind of work` IS ONE OF
    `building a new house or other building`
    `renovating, altering, extending or repairing the house`
    `building a swimming pool, fence, retaining wall or other incidental structure`
    `assembling or securing a relocated house`
    `site work for any of these`
    `demolishing the house`
    `work prescribed as not being building work`

-- One case is one piece of work on one building (the text's unit: "a building permit is in effect for the building work").
DECLARE Work HAS
    `kind` IS A `Kind of work`
    -- s 9(b): "a building permit is not required for the building work under Part 5 or regulations or an order mentioned
    -- in Part 5 Division 1" (s 66(1) regulations; s 67 Ministerial order). The Building Regulations 2012 are not
    -- deposited: a FACT.
    `the regulations or a Ministerial order say it needs no building permit` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 69(1): "A permit is not required for a building or an incidental structure that is to remain erected for no longer
    -- than one month." s 69(2): unless "members of the public normally use" it or "are permitted access".
    `is to remain erected for no longer than one month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `members of the public will use it or be permitted access` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9(c): "the work is done in accordance with a building order".
    `is done in accordance with a building order` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9(a): "a building permit is in effect for the building work".
    `a building permit is in effect for it` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 5(1): "owner, in relation to land held in freehold ... means -- (a) a person whose name is registered as a proprietor of
-- the land; ... (c) a person who holds a prescribed interest in the land". The prescribed interests are in the
-- regulations, not deposited: a FACT.
DECLARE Person HAS
    `is registered as a proprietor of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a prescribed interest in the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 16(c), s 31 "responsible person": "the person who proposes to be named as the builder on the building permit".
    -- An owner-builder is both (s 20(1)(b)(ii): "has owner-builder approval under the Registration Act").
    `is named as the builder on the building permit` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 4(2): a building surveyor is independent if "(a) the building surveyor is neither an owner of the land ..., nor an
-- employee of an owner of the land; and (b) the building surveyor is neither the person who proposes to be named as the
-- builder ..., nor an employee of that person". s 20(1)(d)(i): "entitled under the Registration Act to sign certificates
-- of design compliance" for the kind of building -- a borrowed term, asked as a FACT.
DECLARE Surveyor HAS
    `is an owner of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an employee of an owner of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the proposed builder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an employee of the proposed builder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is entitled under the Registration Act to sign certificates for this kind of building` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is what I plan to do "building work" under the Building Act 2011 (WA) s 3?
GIVEN `the work` IS A Work @desc The work you plan to do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it building work` `the work` IF
    CONSIDER `the work`'s `kind`
    WHEN `demolishing the house` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `work prescribed as not being building work` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 69: the one-month exemption, lost if the public use the structure or may enter it.
GIVEN `the work` IS A Work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the temporary building exemption applies` `the work` IF
        `the work`'s `is to remain erected for no longer than one month`
    AND (NOT `the work`'s `members of the public will use it or be permitted access`)

@export Am I an "owner" of the land under the Building Act 2011 (WA) s 5?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc You, and your interest in the land
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an owner` `me` IF
        `me`'s `is registered as a proprietor of the land`
    OR  `me`'s `holds a prescribed interest in the land`

@export Is my building surveyor an independent building surveyor (s 4)?
GIVEN `the surveyor` IS A Surveyor @desc The building surveyor who signs your certificate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my building surveyor independent` `the surveyor` IF
        (NOT `the surveyor`'s `is an owner of the land`)
    AND (NOT `the surveyor`'s `is an employee of an owner of the land`)
    AND (NOT `the surveyor`'s `is the proposed builder`)
    AND (NOT `the surveyor`'s `is an employee of the proposed builder`)

§§ `s 9, ss 11, 12 -- building permit, and building without one`

-- s 9: "A person must not do building work unless -- (a) a building permit is in effect for the building work; or (b) a
-- building permit is not required for the building work under Part 5 or regulations or an order mentioned in Part 5
-- Division 1; or (c) the work is done in accordance with a building order; or (d) the work is done in the course of taking
-- action under section 118(2)." (s 118(2) is the permit authority itself doing the work; out of the owner's seat.)
@export Do I need a building permit for this work (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 9)?
GIVEN `the work` IS A Work @desc The work you plan to do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I need a building permit` `the work` IF
        `Is it building work` `the work`
    AND (NOT `the work`'s `the regulations or a Ministerial order say it needs no building permit`)
    AND (NOT `the temporary building exemption applies` `the work`)
    AND (NOT `the work`'s `is done in accordance with a building order`)

-- s 11: a defence where the permit "was not in effect because it was suspended under section 35" if the accused "(a) was not
-- aware that an event mentioned in section 35(a) or (b) had occurred ...; and (b) could not reasonably be expected to have
-- known". s 12: a defence for emergency work under ss 78(1)(c), 79(1)(c), 80(1)(c) followed "as soon as practicable" by an
-- application. Both are for the accused to make out; asked as FACTS.
@export Would doing this work be the offence of building without a permit (s 9; defences ss 11, 12)?
GIVEN `the work` IS A Work @desc The work you are doing
      `the permit was suspended and I neither knew nor could reasonably have known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your permit was suspended (the builder ceased or lost registration) without your knowing, or any reasonable way of knowing
      `it was emergency work and I applied for a permit as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was emergency protection work under ss 78-80 and you applied for a permit as soon as practicable afterwards
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would doing the work be an offence` `the work` `the permit was suspended and I neither knew nor could reasonably have known` `it was emergency work and I applied for a permit as soon as practicable` IF
        `Do I need a building permit` `the work`
    AND (NOT `the work`'s `a building permit is in effect for it`)
    AND (NOT `the permit was suspended and I neither knew nor could reasonably have known`)
    AND (NOT `it was emergency work and I applied for a permit as soon as practicable`)

-- The penalty for ss 9, 29(1), 37 and 41: "(a) for a first offence, a fine of $50 000; (b) for a second offence, a fine of
-- $75 000; (c) for a third or subsequent offence, a fine of $100 000 and imprisonment for 12 months."
@export What is the most I can be fined for building without a permit, failing the building standards, or occupying without an occupancy permit, in dollars (ss 9, 37, 41)?
GIVEN `previous offences` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times you have offended against the same section before
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined` `previous offences` IS
    IF `previous offences` EQUALS 0 THEN 50000
    ELSE IF `previous offences` EQUALS 1 THEN 75000
         ELSE 100000

@export For a third or later offence I may also be imprisoned: for how many months at most (ss 9, 37, 41)?
GIVEN `previous offences` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times you have offended against the same section before
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest I can be imprisoned in months` `previous offences` IS
    IF `previous offences` AT LEAST 2 THEN 12 ELSE 0

§§ `ss 14, 16, 17, 19 -- applying, and the certificate of design compliance`

-- s 16: "An application -- ... (b) must name, and be signed by, each owner of the land on which the building ... is, or is
-- proposed to be, located; and (c) must name, and be signed by, the person who proposes to be named as the builder on the
-- building permit".
@export Must I sign the application for the building permit (s 16(b), (c))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc You, and your part in the work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I sign the building permit application` `me` IF
        `Am I an owner` `me`
    OR  `me`'s `is named as the builder on the building permit`

-- s 14(1): a certified application may be made for "a building ... of any classification"; s 14(2): an uncertified
-- application only for "a classification that is prescribed for the purposes of this subsection". The prescribed
-- classifications are in the regulations, not deposited: a FACT.
@export May I make an uncertified application for this building (s 14(2))?
GIVEN `its classification is prescribed for uncertified applications` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations prescribe the building's classification (for example Class 1a, a house) for uncertified applications
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make an uncertified application` `its classification is prescribed for uncertified applications` IF
    `its classification is prescribed for uncertified applications`

DECLARE `Kind of application` IS ONE OF
    `a certified application`
    `an uncertified application`

DECLARE `Where the certificate of design compliance comes from` IS ONE OF
    `I attach it, signed by a building surveyor, with the plans it specifies`
    `the permit authority refers my plans to a building surveyor, who decides whether to sign it`

-- s 16(e): a certified application "must be accompanied by a certificate of design compliance ... that is signed by a
-- building surveyor and complies with section 19"; (h) an uncertified application "must be accompanied by the plans and
-- specifications for consideration by a building surveyor under section 17". s 17(1): the permit authority "must refer to
-- a building surveyor an uncertified application"; (2) the surveyor "must decide whether to sign a certificate of design
-- compliance". s 28(2A): on an uncertified application a copy of the certificate "must also be given to the applicant".
@export Where does my certificate of design compliance come from (ss 16(e), (h), 17)?
GIVEN `the application` IS A `Kind of application` @desc Whether you apply with a certificate already signed (certified) or without (uncertified)
GIVETH A `Where the certificate of design compliance comes from`
DECIDE `Where does my certificate of design compliance come from` `the application` IS
    CONSIDER `the application`
    WHEN `a certified application` THEN `I attach it, signed by a building surveyor, with the plans it specifies`
    WHEN `an uncertified application` THEN `the permit authority refers my plans to a building surveyor, who decides whether to sign it`

§§ `s 20 -- must the permit be granted`

-- s 20(1): the permit authority "must grant the building permit if it is satisfied" of each of (a)-(s), and s 20(2) "must
-- not grant the building permit unless it is satisfied as to each". The matters the owner can state are separate fields;
-- the rest of (g), (h), (j), (l)-(s) (boundaries, other insurance, training levy, heritage, other authorities and prescribed
-- requirements) is one field. Each field is the permit authority's satisfaction, asked as a FACT.
DECLARE `Building permit application` HAS
    -- s 20(1)(a): "the applicant has complied with section 16" (approved form, signatures of every owner and the builder,
    -- prescribed information, plans, technical certificates, fee).
    `complies with section 16, signed by every owner and the builder` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 20(1)(b): the builder is a registered building service contractor, "has owner-builder approval", a public
    -- authority, or a prescribed person.
    `the named builder is registered or has owner-builder approval` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 20(1)(c): "a certificate of design compliance ... complies with section 19" (s 19(3): a statement that the building,
    -- "completed in accordance with the plans and specifications ..., will comply with each applicable building standard").
    `has a certificate of design compliance that complies with section 19` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the surveyor` IS A Surveyor
    -- s 20(1)(e): the certificate "is issued by" a building service contractor entitled under Registration Act s 11.
    `the certificate is issued by an entitled building service contractor` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 20(1)(i): home indemnity insurance under the Home Building Contracts Act 1991 Part 3A Division 2 is in force,
    -- corresponding cover is provided, or neither "is not required".
    `home indemnity insurance is in force or not required` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 20(1)(k): "any building services levy required ... has been paid".
    `the building services levy is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `every other matter in section 20(1) is satisfied (permit authority)` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Must the permit authority grant my building permit (s 20)?
GIVEN `the application` IS A `Building permit application` @desc Your application and what the permit authority is satisfied of
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my building permit be granted` `the application` IF
        `the application`'s `complies with section 16, signed by every owner and the builder`
    AND `the application`'s `the named builder is registered or has owner-builder approval`
    AND `the application`'s `has a certificate of design compliance that complies with section 19`
    AND `the application`'s `the surveyor`'s `is entitled under the Registration Act to sign certificates for this kind of building`
    AND `Is my building surveyor independent` (`the application`'s `the surveyor`)
    AND `the application`'s `the certificate is issued by an entitled building service contractor`
    AND `the application`'s `home indemnity insurance is in force or not required`
    AND `the application`'s `the building services levy is paid`
    AND `the application`'s `every other matter in section 20(1) is satisfied (permit authority)`

§§ `ss 23, 24, 28, 32, 119 -- the decision, the permit, and its life`

-- s 23(1), (2): the permit authority must decide "before the expiration of the period -- (i) that is prescribed ... for the
-- classification of the building ...; and (ii) starting on the day after the application is made". (3) "If the permit
-- authority has not made a decision in the time ... the permit authority is to be taken to have refused". The period is in
-- the regulations, not deposited: an input. Days are counted from the day after the application; a further-information
-- requirement under s 18 restarts the balance, which is not encoded.
@export Is my building permit application taken to have been refused (s 23(3))?
GIVEN `days since I applied` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since you applied, counting from the day after
      `the prescribed period in days` IS A NUMBER @desc The period the regulations prescribe for this classification
      `a decision has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the permit authority has decided
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my application taken to be refused` `days since I applied` `the prescribed period in days` `a decision has been made` IF
        (NOT `a decision has been made`)
    AND `days since I applied` GREATER THAN `the prescribed period in days`

-- s 23(4): if no decision in time, the permit authority "must refund to the applicant the fee" and it "is recoverable ...
-- as a debt due to the applicant". (5): not if it refused to consider the application because a s 18(1) requirement was not
-- met, or if the Heritage Council has not given its advice in time.
@export Must my application fee be refunded because no decision was made in time (s 23(4), (5))?
GIVEN `days since I applied` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since you applied, counting from the day after
      `the prescribed period in days` IS A NUMBER @desc The period the regulations prescribe for this classification
      `a decision has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the permit authority has decided
      `I did not give further information asked for in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authority refused to consider your application because you did not give information it asked for within the time set
      `the Heritage Council's advice is outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application was referred under the Heritage Act 2018 and the advice has not come back in time
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my fee be refunded` `days since I applied` `the prescribed period in days` `a decision has been made` `I did not give further information asked for in time` `the Heritage Council's advice is outstanding` IF
        `Is my application taken to be refused` `days since I applied` `the prescribed period in days` `a decision has been made`
    AND (NOT `I did not give further information asked for in time`)
    AND (NOT `the Heritage Council's advice is outstanding`)

-- s 24(b): written notice of a refusal, "together with those grounds and reasons, and the person's right of review under
-- section 119", "not later than 5 days after making the decision".
@export Within how many days of refusing my building permit must the permit authority give me written notice and its reasons (s 24)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must I be told why I was refused` IS 5

-- s 119: "A person who applies for a building permit ... may apply to the State Administrative Tribunal for a review of the
-- decision of the permit authority -- (a) to refuse to grant a building permit ...; or (b) in relation to a condition".
@export May I ask the State Administrative Tribunal to review a refusal of, or a condition on, my building permit (s 119)?
GIVEN `I applied for the permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were the applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the Tribunal to review` `I applied for the permit` IF `I applied for the permit`

-- s 28(1): "A building permit document must be given to -- (a) the person who is named as the builder ...; (b) each owner
-- of the land".
@export Must I be given the building permit document (s 28(1))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc You, and your part in the work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be given the building permit` `me` IF
        `Am I an owner` `me`
    OR  `me`'s `is named as the builder on the building permit`

-- s 32(1): a permit has effect for "the period set out in the permit", or (2) "If a permit does not set out the period ...
-- 2 years from the day on which it is granted", in either case or "such longer period that is approved" on an extension
-- (not encoded). (4): it ceases on the day the notice of completion is received.
@export For how many years does my building permit have effect (s 32)?
GIVEN `the period set out in the permit, in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The period stated on the permit, in years (0 if none is stated)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `For how many years does my building permit last` `the period set out in the permit, in years` IS
    IF `the period set out in the permit, in years` EQUALS 0 THEN 2
    ELSE `the period set out in the permit, in years`

§§ `ss 33, 34, 37 -- completion`

-- s 33(1): "The responsible person in relation to a permit must, within 7 days of completion of the work ... give notice of
-- completion to a relevant permit authority. Penalty: a fine of $10 000." s 31: the responsible person is "the person named
-- as the builder on the permit". An owner who is not the named builder has no duty; 0 means none.
@export Within how many days of completion must I give the notice of completion (s 33(1))? (0 means it is not my duty)
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc You, and your part in the work
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must I give the notice of completion` `me` IS
    IF `me`'s `is named as the builder on the building permit` THEN 7 ELSE 0

@export What is the most I can be fined for not giving the notice of completion in time, in dollars (s 33(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for not giving notice of completion` IS 10000

-- s 34(3): a builder who gives notice of cessation must, "within 7 days ..., give a copy of the notice to an owner".
@export If my builder stops acting on the permit, within how many days must I be given a copy of the notice of cessation (s 34(3))? (0 means none is owed to me)
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc You, and your interest in the land
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must I get the notice of cessation` `me` IS
    IF `Am I an owner` `me` THEN 7 ELSE 0

-- s 37(1): "The person who is named as the builder on a building permit must ensure, on completion ..., that the building
-- ... complies with each applicable building standard." (2): "Each owner of a building ... in respect of which building
-- work is done without a building permit being in effect for the building work must ensure, on completion ..., that the
-- building ... complies with each applicable building standard."
@export Must I ensure that the completed house complies with every applicable building standard (s 37)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc You, and your part in the work
      `the work` IS A Work @desc The work that was done
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I ensure the finished house meets the building standards` `me` `the work` IF
        (`me`'s `is named as the builder on the building permit` AND `the work`'s `a building permit is in effect for it`)
    OR  (    `Am I an owner` `me`
         AND `Is it building work` `the work`
         AND (NOT `the work`'s `a building permit is in effect for it`))

§§ `ss 40, 41, 46, 47, 51, 54, 63 -- the occupancy permit`

-- s 41(2): "An owner or occupier of a completed building must not occupy or use, or permit the occupation or use of, the
-- building unless -- (a) an occupancy permit, other than a temporary permit, is in effect for the building; or (b) a
-- temporary permit ... has effect for a period after the completion of the building and the occupation or use ... is during
-- that period; or (c) an occupancy permit is not required for the building under Part 5 or regulations or an order
-- mentioned in Part 5 Division 1." (3): for an incomplete building, only (a) a temporary permit or (b) the exemption.
-- s 40: "occupier ... includes a person who occupies or uses the building ... under a lease, tenancy agreement or licence".
-- The Act ITSELF exempts no class of building from s 41: there is no "Class 1" or "house" exception in its text. Exemption
-- comes only from Part 5 (s 69 temporary buildings; ss 70-74, which do not reach a house), from regulations under s 66(5)
-- ("an occupancy permit is not required for a building of a kind specified by the regulations"), or from a Ministerial
-- order under s 67. The Building Regulations 2012 are not deposited, so whether a Class 1a house is such a building is a
-- FACT.
DECLARE Building HAS
    `is completed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an occupancy permit, other than a temporary one, is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 41(1), s 47: "temporary permit means an occupancy permit granted on an application mentioned in section 47"
    -- (an incomplete building); s 41(2)(b) lets its period run past completion.
    `a temporary occupancy permit is in effect now` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the regulations or a Ministerial order say it needs no occupancy permit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is to remain erected for no longer than one month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `members of the public will use it or be permitted access` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the building` IS A Building
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the building is exempt from occupancy permits` `the building` IF
        `the building`'s `the regulations or a Ministerial order say it needs no occupancy permit`
    OR  (    `the building`'s `is to remain erected for no longer than one month`
         AND (NOT `the building`'s `members of the public will use it or be permitted access`))

@export Must my new house have an occupancy permit before we move in (s 41; s 66(5); s 69)?
GIVEN `the building` IS A Building @desc Your house, and whether the regulations exempt it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the house have an occupancy permit` `the building` IF
    NOT `the building is exempt from occupancy permits` `the building`

@export May we move in, or let someone else live in or use the house (s 41(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the building` IS A Building @desc Your house, whether it is finished, and what permit it has
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May we move in` `the building` IF
    IF `the building`'s `is completed`
    THEN    `the building`'s `an occupancy permit, other than a temporary one, is in effect`
         OR `the building`'s `a temporary occupancy permit is in effect now`
         OR `the building is exempt from occupancy permits` `the building`
    ELSE    `the building`'s `a temporary occupancy permit is in effect now`
         OR `the building is exempt from occupancy permits` `the building`

@export Would moving in, or letting someone else live in the house, be an offence (s 41)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc You, and your interest in the land
      `I occupy it under a lease, tenancy agreement or licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live in or use the house as a tenant or licensee (an occupier, s 40)
      `the building` IS A Building @desc Your house, whether it is finished, and what permit it has
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would moving in be an offence` `me` `I occupy it under a lease, tenancy agreement or licence` `the building` IF
        (`Am I an owner` `me` OR `I occupy it under a lease, tenancy agreement or licence`)
    AND (NOT `May we move in` `the building`)

DECLARE `Kind of occupancy permit application` IS ONE OF
    `for a completed building (s 46)`
    `for an incomplete building (s 47)`
    `for a building with unauthorised work (s 51)`

DECLARE `Compliance certificate` IS ONE OF
    `a certificate of construction compliance`
    `a certificate of building compliance`

-- s 54(2): "An application mentioned in section 46 or 47 must be accompanied by a certificate of construction compliance
-- that complies with section 56." (3): "An application of any other kind must be accompanied by a certificate of building
-- compliance that complies with section 57." Both are signed by a building surveyor (ss 56(1), 57(1)).
@export Which certificate must accompany my occupancy permit application (s 54(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the application` IS A `Kind of occupancy permit application` @desc What the occupancy permit is for
GIVETH A `Compliance certificate`
DECIDE `Which certificate must accompany my occupancy permit application` `the application` IS
    CONSIDER `the application`
    WHEN `for a completed building (s 46)` THEN `a certificate of construction compliance`
    WHEN `for an incomplete building (s 47)` THEN `a certificate of construction compliance`
    WHEN `for a building with unauthorised work (s 51)` THEN `a certificate of building compliance`

-- s 54(1)(b): an application must be "signed by each owner of the land on which the building ... is located"; s 63(a):
-- the occupancy permit "must be given to -- (a) each owner of the building".
@export Must I sign the occupancy permit application, and be given the permit (ss 54(1)(b), 63)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Person @desc You, and your interest in the land
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I sign the occupancy permit application` `me` IF `Am I an owner` `me`

§§ `s 133 -- how long I can be prosecuted for`

DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    `building without a building permit (s 9)`
    `an owner's completed building not meeting the standards (s 37(2))`
    `occupying without an occupancy permit (s 41)`
    `not giving notice of completion (s 33)`

-- s 133(3): "A prosecution for an offence against section 9, 10, 29(1) or (2), 37(1) or (2), ... may be commenced within 6
-- years after the offence was allegedly committed, but not later." (4): "A prosecution for any other offence against this
-- Act may be commenced within 3 years".
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the limitation period in years` `the offence` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `building without a building permit (s 9)` THEN 6
    WHEN `an owner's completed building not meeting the standards (s 37(2))` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 3

@export Can I still be prosecuted for this offence (s 133(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence alleged
      `years since the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years ago the offence was allegedly committed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still be prosecuted` `the offence` `years since the offence` IF
    `years since the offence` AT MOST `the limitation period in years` `the offence`
